ion of any Bishop  is to sit rock-like stationary in a  chair a cathedra to be a focus of unity  for the flock which he regulates with  his shepherd's crook by rod and thy  staff they comfort me  the Petrin principle provides for fixity  certainty a still point in a turning  world but st. Paul is the missionary the  apostle to the Gentiles who goes all  over the Mediterranean spreading the  word founding new churches tackling  practical problems developing new  theological understandings firing off  letters left right and center and once  even challenging Peter to his face and  this all line principle is important  because I recognize that not everyone at  Hillsdale calls themselves Christian you  may not be much interested in the life  of the new chapel when it comes you have  other fish to fry  you may even wish respectfully to  challenge this or that aspect of hills  dales priorities that's a good role to  fulfill in a community every human  organization needs Paul's as well as  Peters Paul as as well as Petra's if it  was all about Peter things would petrify  if it was all about Paul things would be  appalling  you need both you need both you need the  rock in Rome and the one who roams and  rocks to principles in tension with each  other  respecting each other but both seeking  one ultimate goal serving the same  beating heart the heart itself is more  important than whether the blood within  it happens to be a being or flowing true  religion therefore needs to be  understood in two senses it both does  and is theirs the particular religious  impulse a function that tying back  together but then there's religion  itself the overall pattern the continual  rhythmic regular process of now tying  back now loosening up  neither Peter nor Paul with an end in  himself each was a servant of Christ the  two pointed to the one the unity beyond  themselves and that greater unity that  final law ultimate real igg amounting is  why it's so fitting that this new chapel  will be known as Christ's chapel for  Christ is the one in whom all things  hold together both the tightening and  the loosening both the systolic and the  diastolic both the rock and the rocking  today we break new ground we challenge  the rock so to speak we do something  very poor line very an elliptical  scattering earth this way and that but  we do so with an aim in mind to develop  and extend that ground into a new unity  and enlarged oneness we have a Petrin  end in view there is a time to scatter  stones and a time to gather stones  together may earth be better and  heaven be richer from a life and labor  of Hillsdale College Armand  [Applause]
 

